WEBVTT

00:17.160 --> 00:19.490
If you turn me into a cyborg

00:17.160 --> 00:19.490
Kaizou suru nara

00:19.700 --> 00:22.160
install a self-destruct device

00:19.700 --> 00:22.160
Jibaku souchi wa

00:22.330 --> 00:25.870
as an option

00:22.330 --> 00:25.870
opshon tsukete kure

00:27.540 --> 00:28.670
If I

00:27.540 --> 00:28.670
Kimi o

00:28.840 --> 00:31.260
can't protect you

00:28.840 --> 00:31.260
Mamotte yarenai nara

00:31.420 --> 00:32.550
living

00:31.420 --> 00:32.550
Ikiteru

00:32.720 --> 00:33.840
has no meaning

00:32.720 --> 00:33.840
imi nai

00:34.010 --> 00:36.760
at all to me

00:34.010 --> 00:36.760
ore na no dakara

00:37.720 --> 00:40.180
Even if I had my erased memories back

00:37.720 --> 00:40.180
Kesareta kioku ni sae mo

00:40.310 --> 00:42.770
I wouldn't remember the two of us

00:40.310 --> 00:42.770
futari no omoide nai

00:43.020 --> 00:47.690
That's my one-sided and self-destructive love

00:43.020 --> 00:47.690
Sou wansaido jibaku no aisa

00:48.690 --> 00:50.650
I am still young

00:48.690 --> 00:50.650
Atara wakai

00:50.820 --> 00:54.110
but willing to exchange my life for yours

00:50.820 --> 00:54.110
Inochi o hikikaeshita tote kamawanai

00:55.280 --> 00:56.910
I'll become

00:55.280 --> 00:56.910
Kimi no

00:57.490 --> 00:59.160
your hero

00:57.490 --> 00:59.160
hiiroo ni naru

00:59.450 --> 01:01.740
If you are

00:59.450 --> 01:01.740
kimi ga akutou de

01:01.950 --> 01:06.120
kidnapped by villains

01:01.950 --> 01:06.120
saratte kureta nara

01:06.500 --> 01:10.540
You can upgrade me as you please

01:06.500 --> 01:10.540
katte ni kaizou shite mo ii ze

01:10.960 --> 01:14.550
[Elesa-Suimasen] presents

01:11.420 --> 01:14.550
Katte Ni

01:11.420 --> 01:14.550
Kaizou

01:14.970 --> 01:19.800
Second year student of Torauma High School, Katsu Kaizō is a cyborg.

01:19.800 --> 01:23.560
Attacked by mysterious people and left close to death with severe injuries

01:23.560 --> 01:26.690
he was turned into a cyborg by genius scientist Saien Suzu

01:26.690 --> 01:28.980
which saved his life.

01:28.980 --> 01:31.360
She brought along with her the underling Tsubouchi Chitan

01:31.360 --> 01:34.150
along with whom Kaizō continues his fight.

01:35.110 --> 01:38.610
Or at least, this is what he imagines.

01:54.920 --> 01:57.590
Look at this magnificent crawl stroke!

02:00.050 --> 02:02.140
Wh-what's this sound...?

02:02.390 --> 02:07.560
A water pressure rise of 0.5%! A water temperature rise of 0.2%! A water level rise of 0.5cm!

02:07.560 --> 02:08.390
This is...

02:08.810 --> 02:10.150
An erection!!

02:11.560 --> 02:13.900
Somebody in here has an erection!!

02:15.400 --> 02:16.150
Who is it?

02:16.150 --> 02:17.190
It's not me!

02:17.190 --> 02:18.240
I-it's not me, either!

02:20.490 --> 02:23.120
Watch my wonderful breaststroke!

02:35.880 --> 02:37.670
So he's the one with the boner!?

02:37.670 --> 02:40.050
What unworthy perverted behavior for an underling!

02:48.640 --> 02:50.060
A rocket cock...!

02:51.770 --> 02:54.730
The thing's chasing after me on it's own!!

02:55.070 --> 03:00.070
No way, a penis that can move on it's own! How can the likes of that underling have such powers?!

03:00.490 --> 03:03.070
How... how cruel...

03:33.310 --> 03:34.480
The bloody...!

03:34.480 --> 03:36.820
The bloody swimming trunks!

03:42.400 --> 03:44.160
Spirit Begone

03:42.400 --> 03:44.160
Evil Spirit Begone

03:42.400 --> 03:44.160
Do Not Enter

03:47.450 --> 03:49.790
To think that this rumor actually was true...

03:49.790 --> 03:53.620
There are certainly things in this world that can't be explained by science.

03:53.620 --> 03:55.670
O Great Buddha...

03:57.460 --> 04:01.300
S...so cruel...

04:04.930 --> 04:05.930
Torauma Ginza

04:13.940 --> 04:15.310
Senpai!

04:18.520 --> 04:21.440
Kaizō-senpai, long time no see!

04:21.740 --> 04:24.110
Where's France!?

04:24.400 --> 04:27.870
Hey, Nukata! How's it going?

04:27.870 --> 04:29.490
Just great!

04:29.830 --> 04:32.080
Too bad you couldn't get on the national team.

04:33.080 --> 04:35.870
They just can't understand my passes.

04:36.250 --> 04:42.090
Nothing you can do about it. Your killer passing just doesn't fit with the current Japanese team.

04:42.090 --> 04:43.920
Well, there's still 2002.

04:44.050 --> 04:49.930
2002 is no good. 2002 won't be in France after all...

04:50.930 --> 04:53.770
You bastard! So you just want to go to France!?

04:53.770 --> 04:56.020
But isn't it just wonderful?

04:56.190 --> 04:59.270
I hate to admit it, but I definitely have to agree with how awesome France is.

04:59.270 --> 05:05.400
The Colosseum, the Parthenon, Big Ben... all tourist spots that are up there with Ueno Zoo.

05:05.400 --> 05:08.200
Uh...those aren't in France...

05:08.200 --> 05:13.000
Whatever, you're still Japanese! I won't let you extol France any further!

05:17.540 --> 05:22.250
I'm sorry, Senpai. I'm the one at fault.

05:22.250 --> 05:25.260
I won't extol France any more.

05:25.880 --> 05:27.550
France...

05:29.640 --> 05:30.140
Fashion.

05:30.140 --> 05:30.640
The meals are creamy and yummy.

05:30.640 --> 05:31.140
They talk smart.

05:31.140 --> 05:31.640
The afternoons are filled with <i>ennui</i>.

05:31.890 --> 05:33.180
I totally hate you!

05:33.180 --> 05:34.520
Weren't you just going on about it!?

05:34.980 --> 05:37.230
Let's give up on France already.

05:37.230 --> 05:39.440
I guess you just didn't look at the coach?

05:40.060 --> 05:42.770
I hate that coach.

05:43.280 --> 05:44.030
Because...

05:46.530 --> 05:48.610
His face... it's so not French!

05:48.610 --> 05:50.030
You're talking about it AGAIN!?

05:50.570 --> 05:52.280
What are you up to?

05:53.450 --> 05:54.870
Oh, the Professor and Umi.

05:54.870 --> 05:56.500
An acquaintance of yours, Kaizō?

05:56.500 --> 05:59.290
This is Nukata, my former kouhai from Genius Cram School!

05:59.290 --> 06:00.460
Hi there!

06:00.460 --> 06:02.040
Genius Cram School?

06:02.040 --> 06:04.960
It's the cram school Kaizō used to go to.

06:05.420 --> 06:12.220
The Genius Cram School consisted entirely of gifted children and was a Cram School by Geniuses, for Geniuses.

06:12.550 --> 06:18.230
But Kaizō, who had hit his head, combined two strange chemicals in the machine room

06:18.230 --> 06:22.480
which caused a huge explosion engulfing three neighboring buildings on either side!

06:22.480 --> 06:24.230
The Genius Cram School collapsed.

06:25.070 --> 06:29.820
And so, the half-baked geniuses who had previously gone there

06:29.820 --> 06:33.740
did not know what to do with their powers and became abnormal.

06:34.160 --> 06:41.500
I'm Nukata, former student of the Genius Cram School's soccer course and midfielder for the J-League team "Bon Soirrée Yonohon".

06:41.960 --> 06:45.250
He's one of those high school J-Leaguers that are so <i>en vogue</i> right now.

06:45.250 --> 06:46.670
Be still my heart...

06:46.670 --> 06:47.880
What's wrong, Nukata?

06:50.340 --> 06:51.720
So...French!

06:51.720 --> 06:52.930
AGAIN, you bastard?!

06:52.930 --> 06:56.850
But that feathered hair, it looks so French!

06:56.850 --> 07:00.140
The French aren't even all that these days...

07:03.730 --> 07:07.070
I don't want to hear it from someone so un-French.

07:07.820 --> 07:10.610
What about me is non-French!?

07:10.610 --> 07:14.160
Also, what's the big difference between the Chief and me!?

07:14.160 --> 07:16.990
I don't get it, but I'm really pissed!!

07:17.290 --> 07:20.460
I'll show you how French I am!!

07:20.460 --> 07:23.210
Isn't it okay to not be French?

07:23.210 --> 07:27.210
Everyone take a look at today's bentō! Tri-colored just like the French flag!!

07:30.090 --> 07:33.840
This green in no way resembles the <i>bleu</i> of France!

07:33.840 --> 07:35.930
The hell are you talking about!?!

07:35.930 --> 07:41.060
Isn't the fact that a high school student made such a three-colored bentō more of a problem?

07:43.850 --> 07:48.690
By the way, Nukata, I've been wanting to see your Killer Pass for quite some time.

07:48.690 --> 07:51.110
I want to see it, too!

07:51.110 --> 07:53.570
For real? A French-like person wants to see it!?

07:53.570 --> 07:57.200
All right, go for it, Nukata!

07:57.200 --> 07:58.200
Yes sir!

08:01.960 --> 08:03.830
Killer Pass!!

08:03.830 --> 08:04.960
Where's it gonna go?

08:32.070 --> 08:34.740
As usual, a great pass.

08:34.740 --> 08:38.740
Passes from his feet always bring calamities.

08:38.740 --> 08:40.700
You can't let a guy like that just do his thing!!

08:40.910 --> 08:43.870
Seems I'm in top form today!

08:43.870 --> 08:45.460
Let's bang some more passes!

08:45.750 --> 08:47.960
Killer Pass!

08:47.960 --> 08:49.920
[Note: These three pages are from Katte ni Kaizou Chapter 1]

08:49.920 --> 08:52.710
Ah, it's finally finished!

08:52.710 --> 08:54.760
Now I can sleep for the first time in three days!

08:56.970 --> 08:59.470
[Note: The symbol on his hat is the 'me' (米) from 'Kumeta' (久米田)]

08:59.890 --> 09:00.850
I'm killing myself.

09:00.850 --> 09:02.220
What should we do?

09:02.600 --> 09:03.730
Let's leave him alone.

09:03.730 --> 09:05.230
Torauma Park

09:05.560 --> 09:08.940
Oh god, I'm gonna crap my pants!

09:08.940 --> 09:12.360
Ah, I made it!

09:12.360 --> 09:14.110
That was close...

09:32.380 --> 09:33.840
Own Goal!

09:40.890 --> 09:42.970
We can see them, we can see them!

09:58.490 --> 10:00.700
Back Charge! Red Card!

10:00.950 --> 10:08.500
Hey, take it out!!

10:03.700 --> 10:05.830
Hey, don't hold onto it!!

10:17.380 --> 10:18.630
Three Back!

10:19.760 --> 10:21.800
Get it OUT!!

10:21.800 --> 10:23.510
I told you, don't hold onto it!!

10:23.890 --> 10:27.770
My pass can even cause a triple back line, that means I can't stop!

10:28.060 --> 10:29.230
Killer Pass!

10:29.440 --> 10:30.480
Don't hold onto it!!

10:33.730 --> 10:35.190
Get it OUT!

10:38.900 --> 10:40.610
I'm dying here!!

10:44.830 --> 10:48.620
Th...the city...

10:48.620 --> 10:51.170
Yeah, this really is one frightening Killer Pass.

10:51.170 --> 10:53.960
Isn't it your fault that we have this half-assed genius here?!!

10:53.960 --> 10:55.800
Take responsibility and make him stop!

10:55.800 --> 10:57.090
Impossible.

10:57.590 --> 11:00.840
Now that he's on a roll, nobody can stop him now.

11:00.840 --> 11:02.840
Not even Wakabayashi-kun

11:00.840 --> 11:02.840
[TL Note: Wakabayashi is a character from Captain Tsubasa]

11:03.090 --> 11:04.300
Huh, who?

11:07.600 --> 11:11.850
What's with all this noise...? Don't disturb my reading.

11:12.850 --> 11:14.980
Somebody stop him!

11:14.980 --> 11:16.650
Killer Pass!

11:32.670 --> 11:33.630
Here, take it.

11:33.630 --> 11:35.250
H...he stopped him.

11:35.250 --> 11:37.960
Chitan-kun, you're pretty good at soccer, aren't you?

11:37.960 --> 11:41.800
Huh? I haven't even played it once.

11:38.550 --> 11:41.800
<i>Magazine: Railway Spirit</i>

11:42.010 --> 11:43.180
Seriously?

11:43.180 --> 11:47.720
I'm not interested in it. When they show it live on TV, animes start later.

11:47.720 --> 11:49.560
I totally hate soccer!

11:49.770 --> 11:54.440
God doesn't only give people the powers they desire.

11:54.440 --> 12:01.570
If he had become a soccer player, he would have had a talent to shock the world with,

12:01.950 --> 12:08.620
but for him, who has no connection to soccer at all, this gift will never be demonstrated.

12:08.910 --> 12:09.830
What?

12:10.160 --> 12:12.290
The hell, that makes me sick!

12:12.290 --> 12:15.540
You're the driver!

12:15.540 --> 12:18.920
And I'm the conductor!

12:31.730 --> 12:33.560
Seems I bought a bit too much.

12:34.020 --> 12:38.020
But this year's fall collection is really cute...!

12:40.480 --> 12:41.650
Kaizō!

12:42.990 --> 12:46.740
Your timing is perfect! Help me carry my bags!

12:46.740 --> 12:51.120
Aren't you late, Umi? If you've been summoned, you should show up immediately.

12:51.120 --> 12:52.580
Summoned?

12:53.080 --> 12:56.420
Chief and Chitan-kun, were you summoned too?

12:56.420 --> 12:59.460
Yeah, I was forced to come!

12:59.460 --> 13:03.670
It's okay, this is sure to be entertaining!

13:03.670 --> 13:08.390
Lately, mysterious incidents have been happening over and over in this neighborhood.

13:08.390 --> 13:10.260
Huh? Mysterious incidents?

13:10.260 --> 13:13.100
That's right. Repeated cases of the "Sailor Suit Collar Demon"!

13:14.930 --> 13:18.440
That scream, it's... beautiful and popular class president Yamada-san!

13:21.190 --> 13:23.110
Great Demon King of Fashion!?

13:27.070 --> 13:28.360
How mean!

13:28.950 --> 13:33.240
The collar was starched stiff with spray glue!?

13:33.240 --> 13:35.460
Who would do such a thing?

13:35.460 --> 13:38.830
Spray glue... starching the collar...

13:38.830 --> 13:41.290
Speaking of Paris... it's the city of fashion...

13:41.290 --> 13:42.630
That means...

13:42.630 --> 13:43.840
It can't be!

13:43.840 --> 13:49.340
Heh heh heh! Originally, sailor suits were all worn with the collar standing up stylishly like that!

13:49.590 --> 13:52.760
So <i>you're</i> the "Sailor Suit Collar Demon"!

13:52.760 --> 13:56.060
It's... Oshare-sensei!

13:52.760 --> 13:56.060
[TL Note: <i>oshare</i> means stylish or fashionable]

13:56.060 --> 13:58.270
An acquaintance of yours, Kaizō-kun?

14:00.440 --> 14:07.650
This is Mario-sensei, the current head of the "Tokyo Mood School", and a former student in the Genius Cram School's Clothing and Accessories Program!

14:07.650 --> 14:09.780
He's the master who taught me fashion sense!

14:10.160 --> 14:12.700
The Genius Cram School again?!

14:12.700 --> 14:17.960
This is great timing, I was just thinking of asking you about the Fall fashions!

14:17.960 --> 14:20.540
Oh, well done, well done!

14:20.540 --> 14:25.000
Wait a second! Why are you making sailor suit collars stand up?!

14:25.000 --> 14:28.880
I was just educating them on the original way to wear them stylishly.

14:29.180 --> 14:32.510
Wearing them like this could never be right!

14:32.800 --> 14:37.140
You know that sailor suits were originally worn by sailors, yes?

14:37.140 --> 14:40.400
That being the case, then what do you think the collar was for?

14:44.230 --> 14:50.660
When you hold up the collar like this, you can still easily hear your colleagues' voices across the deck, even with all the noise around!

14:50.660 --> 14:52.070
This is true.

14:52.200 --> 14:56.790
Which is why wearing a sailor suit with the collar standing up is the correct way to wear it stylishly.

14:56.790 --> 14:59.000
As expected of you, Oshare-sensei!!

14:59.210 --> 15:04.090
There is a special beauty in the making of fashion.

15:04.340 --> 15:08.380
Isn't it fine if it's cute, even if you don't wear it the right way?

15:08.630 --> 15:11.720
What, Kaizō, is this your girlfriend?

15:11.720 --> 15:17.140
That's your business, but wouldn't it be better to go out with a girl who has better taste?

15:18.560 --> 15:22.770
I'm also utterly depressed about Umi not having any fashion sense.

15:22.770 --> 15:23.980
WHAT WAS THAT?!

15:23.980 --> 15:26.650
How exactly do I have no taste?!

15:26.650 --> 15:32.160
Well then I ask you, what purpose do you think the plaid pattern on that skirt was for?

15:32.160 --> 15:35.700
What purpose? Isn't it just a normal pattern?

15:35.700 --> 15:38.620
Plaid patterns were made for the identification of corpses!

15:38.910 --> 15:42.330
In Europe in the Middle Ages, even when those killed in battle had become a skeleton,

15:42.330 --> 15:46.340
you could identify the dead person and where they were from by the plaid they wore.

15:46.340 --> 15:48.300
Edward!

15:49.090 --> 15:50.630
This is also true, actually.

15:50.920 --> 15:54.890
That means plaid patterns were costumes for those who were prepared to die!

15:54.890 --> 15:57.640
Are you prepared to die?!

15:57.810 --> 16:01.770
So you're telling me I'm not allowed to wear plaid if I'm not ready to die?!

16:01.770 --> 16:06.650
Well, it might be a little rude to say this to someone who has no fashion sense.

16:08.780 --> 16:09.980
It's okay, it's okay...

16:16.320 --> 16:17.700
Milanese!

16:17.700 --> 16:20.700
The Professor really does have Milanese style, doesn't she?

16:20.700 --> 16:24.330
That feathered hair, it's just so Milan!

16:24.330 --> 16:28.500
Well, I can't deny it's Milanese style.

16:29.340 --> 16:31.590
You should absolutely start a fashionable relationship with me!

16:31.590 --> 16:37.100
Why is it always the Chief? First, she's French, now she's Milanese?!

16:37.100 --> 16:43.980
There, there, if you try hard, even though Milan-style might be impossible for you, Midousuji-style might be possible!

16:37.100 --> 16:43.980
[TL Note: Midousuji is a high-class shopping street in Osaka]

16:43.980 --> 16:48.400
You're obviously clueless, so just ask me anything about fashion!

16:48.400 --> 16:51.110
So you really know anything, huh?

16:51.110 --> 16:54.650
Okay, so what's that little pocket on jeans for?

16:54.860 --> 16:56.660
Th...that's, w-well...

16:57.280 --> 17:00.830
Oh, so you don't know...?

17:00.830 --> 17:04.000
There's no need for me to answer this. You tell her, Kaizō-kun.

17:04.210 --> 17:06.290
Got it, Oshare-sensei!

17:06.290 --> 17:09.790
You use that pocket for keeping seeds in!

17:10.090 --> 17:12.260
Seeds..? Why?

17:13.550 --> 17:17.840
Cowboys in Western movies often wear those jeans, right?

17:18.680 --> 17:23.810
In the wasteland, they sow the seeds they had kept.

17:24.390 --> 17:26.390
For the children of the future.

17:26.730 --> 17:29.020
Then they finally sprout...

17:29.020 --> 17:30.190
and become a tree...

17:30.190 --> 17:31.110
then a forest...

17:31.520 --> 17:37.490
thus letting our beautiful green planet earth recover once more. For sure. Save The Earth.

17:37.490 --> 17:38.910
What do you mean, "For sure"?!

17:38.910 --> 17:40.910
Don't just say random crap!

17:40.910 --> 17:45.910
And here I had thought they were for storing upper teeth that had fallen out.

17:45.910 --> 17:49.380
Now even you're saying incomprehensible nonsense, Chief?!

17:49.380 --> 17:51.500
If one of your upper teeth fell out

17:51.500 --> 17:52.750
you could put it there.

17:53.250 --> 17:56.420
I've also had a question like that for a long time.

17:56.420 --> 17:58.550
Hm? What is it? Tell me.

17:58.550 --> 18:02.560
That netting on the inside of a cap, what's it for?

18:02.810 --> 18:06.850
That's for shutting yourself away in your own world.

18:06.850 --> 18:08.350
Your own world!?

18:08.770 --> 18:12.440
When you're the first one to get caught in a game like "Kick the Can", you feel lonely, right?

18:12.440 --> 18:18.360
That's when you lower the visor and imagine... a bright future.

18:18.360 --> 18:19.990
Why a bright future?

18:19.990 --> 18:22.870
Speaking of which, those camouflage pants.

18:23.080 --> 18:25.830
Did you know why they exist, before you put them on?

18:25.830 --> 18:31.380
Er... isn't the camouflage to make it harder for your enemies to find you?

18:31.380 --> 18:32.170
Nope.

18:33.290 --> 18:34.250
Those were

18:34.250 --> 18:36.510
made to conceal embarrassing stains!

18:36.960 --> 18:37.920
Stains...?

18:38.380 --> 18:42.430
Camouflage originates from military briefs.

18:42.430 --> 18:47.810
In the battlefield, you had no change of clothes, so you needed to wear the same pair of briefs again and again.

18:48.270 --> 18:50.600
Doing that, embarrassing stains were sure to appear.

18:50.980 --> 18:53.730
This also affected the morale of the troops.

18:54.070 --> 18:56.730
To camouflage these embarrassing spots

18:57.240 --> 19:00.240
briefs for military use were officially approved!

18:57.610 --> 19:00.240
Approved

19:00.240 --> 19:06.240
By the way, these brown, yellow, and black desert-colored camouflage pants like I also use regularly, are the most popular!

19:06.580 --> 19:08.790
Aren't those real stains?!

19:09.120 --> 19:14.960
When you think about it, if there are girls without standing collars, you will see there are also a lot of girls with a strong talent for crisis management.

19:14.960 --> 19:16.710
What are you trying to say?

19:18.090 --> 19:19.510
Those loose socks!

19:19.760 --> 19:21.760
What about loose socks?

19:21.760 --> 19:24.760
In case of emergency, they blow up like an airbag!

19:25.350 --> 19:27.060
By the way, possible emergencies are:

19:27.060 --> 19:29.480
Being chased by somebody with a leg fetish.

19:29.480 --> 19:32.480
Sitting with your knees drawn up so your panties are visible.

19:32.690 --> 19:37.360
When you're about to drown – in all these cases, they expand and save you from danger.

19:37.360 --> 19:41.360
In short, this is the ideal fashion for high school girls!

19:41.360 --> 19:44.320
Don't use an embarrassing drawing of me as the example!

19:47.240 --> 19:51.540
<i>You</i>, do you know the real purpose of a necktie?!

